abstract:
  A read-only, passive scanner that checks a REDCap host for exposure
  to and compromise by CVE-2026-90817, the unauthenticated survey-endpoint
  remote-code-execution vulnerability abused by the XMRig cryptomining
  campaign. It compares the installed REDCap version against the patched
  releases and hunts the documented indicators of compromise (known
  dropper file hash, miner staging, masquerading processes, local miner
  API, attacker-IP connections, cron/SSH/profile persistence, and
  anti-forensics) without sending any HTTP requests or reproducing the
  exploit. It distinguishes exploit-shaped survey-passthru requests (the
  DataImportController sink, or any controller reached through a
  double-encoded index.php) from legitimate REDCap traffic, feeds the
  attacker IPs it finds back through the logs and host state, and
  correlates attack timestamps in the web-server logs against the
  mitigation date to judge compromise likelihood.
